      "pronunciationText": "Last time, the model of the atom changed three times, each time because of evidence that didn't fit. Your own investigations work the same way. Remember the sand and salt mixture, where the recovered masses added up to more than a hundred percent? That extra wasn't a maths mistake. It was new evidence, and it changed the question, from how much salt is there, to was the sand really dry? Today, we'll build a chemistry question and a hypothesis, then let new evidence improve them.",
