      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "Next comes a hypothesis, a testable prediction with a reason from what we already know. A useful pattern is if, then, because. If blue copper sulfate crystals are heated until their mass stops changing, then they'll lose thirty-six point one percent of their mass, because the formula shows that water is thirty-six point one percent of the mass, and heating drives the water off. The reason is the part that makes it more than a guess. If, then, because: the because is the chemistry.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
