      ],
      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "Group B is a method problem. The blue patches show water was still there, so they didn't heat until the mass stopped changing, which our hypothesis already requires. It doesn't challenge the hypothesis, but it tells us that time matters. Group C is different. They did heat until the mass was steady, and they still lost far more than the water. Black solid means the copper sulfate itself broke down. So the because was incomplete, heating doesn't always drive off only water. When evidence doesn't fit, ask what it challenges: the method, the prediction, or the reason.",
