          "score": 0
        }
      ],
      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "One good question: how does the volume of water used affect the percentage of salt recovered from the mixture? A hypothesis: if more water is used, then more salt is recovered, because more water can dissolve more salt, leaving less behind in the sand. More water is better, is the classic slip. It names nothing to measure, and gives no reason.",
