        }
      ],
      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Recovery rises from twenty to forty millilitres, then stays at about seventy percent. Forty millilitres can dissolve about fourteen grams, so by then, all the salt has dissolved. So modify it. If more water is used, the salt recovered increases until all the salt dissolves, then stays the same, because extra water has no more salt to dissolve. Ignoring the last two results because they don't fit is the classic mistake. Evidence that doesn't fit is what improves the hypothesis.",
